ProsperoSunshine: what each session really sends, for the app's list of streams

The control socket's STREAMS shows what a client asked for and what the capture delivers. It adds what reaches the
network: the video bytes sent (counted per batch, FEC and encryption prefix included), how often the client asked for an
IDR or to invalidate reference frames after a loss, and the round-trip time of the control connection. The control thread
copies the RTT from the ENet peer, since the control socket reads from another thread where the peer may be gone.

--- a/src/rtsp.h
+++ b/src/rtsp.h
@@ -156,6 +156,9 @@
     int dynamic_range;  ///< Color depth the client asked for: 0 = 8-bit, 1 = 10-bit.
     std::chrono::steady_clock::time_point started;  ///< When the session started.
     int gamepads;  ///< Virtual gamepads the client has now.
+    std::uint64_t video_bytes = 0;  ///< Video bytes sent so far, FEC included.
+    std::uint32_t recoveries = 0;  ///< Times the client asked for an IDR or to invalidate reference frames.
+    std::uint32_t rtt_ms = 0;  ///< Round-trip time of the control connection, 0 until known.
   };
 
